  "query_preview": "..\nIsolated showers tonight across Guam and Rota are expected to \ncontinue for the whole forecast period with the exception of \nscattered island effect showers in the afternoon Wednesday. For the \nTinian and Saipan, a trough will continue to move through the region\nand bring scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms tonight,\nbecoming isolated Wednesday. Showers will likely remain isolated \nuntil Friday when scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms return \nupon the passage of Typhoon In-fa somewhere to the north through the\nfar northern CNMI anywhere from just north of Saipan to Maug island.\nShowers for Tinian and Saipan will likely return to isolated for the\nrest of the forecast period by Saturday. Current Typhoon In-Fa is \nexpected to make it's closest point of approach sometime Friday. \nBreezy conditions can be expected for Tinian and Saipan Friday with \nsustained winds up to 30 mph and gusts to 45 mph. The current JTWC \ntrack puts only a 10-20% chance of tropical storm sustained winds for\nTinian and Saipan. This situation remains highly uncertain and will \ncontinue to be monitored closely for any potential changes. See the \n\"Tropical Systems\" section for more details.",
